From 65a38a650a9c812a1d61c27c9a77fe5b5b248142 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:30:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] Android: own the Vulkan surface; Vulkan is the default
 canvas again

Qt destroyed its VkSurfaceKHR from the Android UI thread whenever a
window's surface went away, while the render thread still polled it
(crash on Mali when the symbol chooser closed). The surface is now made
by us on the window's android.view.Surface, which the loader keeps
referenced, so a vanished window reports SURFACE_LOST/OUT_OF_DATE and the
render thread rebuilds it. Windows register in a process-wide set so a
surface is never made from a deleted window. Cairo is an opt-out.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
